     must answer one docker version within ENGINE_PROBE_SECONDS (15), as make image asks it (tasks.md T167), or the
     step fails, naming the timeout or docker's exit status, and builds nothing: docker's client sets no limit of its
     own, so an engine that takes the connection and never answers would hold the gate there. Then the gateway's
     image, outside compose, as make up builds it (tasks.md T184), as h4reet-gateway:<SHA> with the engine's proxy;
     then, when the export has apps/web/Dockerfile, the room's, as make up builds prod's (spec 002), as
     h4reet-web:<SHA> without drafts and with the Dockerfile's own empty policy; then the compose images;
   - matrix-e: stage E, when the branch touches deploy/agents-engine/ or .claude/settings.json. It is Heavy, so it
     waits (PENDING) for --prove, which runs deploy/agents-engine/engine.sh prove;
   - agent-config-evals: the behavioral tier, when the branch touches CLAUDE.md, REVIEW.md, .claude/,
     evals/agent-config/ (its history aside), or the Claude Code pin: the main tree's evals/agent-config/behavioral.py,
     loaded into this process like check_corpus, whose status reads the export's cases, thresholds, history, and
     trigger files as data and starts nothing; in export mode it walks the tree and never runs git. An entry counts
     only when this machine attests its exact bytes (make evals-agent-config writes the SHA-256 under
     ~/.local/state/h4reet, which agent sessions can't write), and the newest attested run for the export's trigger
     hash decides: PASS, FAIL, or PENDING when none has run (the Author runs make evals-agent-config REF=<branch> from
     main's checkout and commits the entry). A file that doesn't load fails. Before main has the tier (T094), this
     step is SKIP naming it.
5. eval-history: each history entry the branch adds is posted once to prod's x004 as the h4.devtime.eval.* gauges
   (contracts/telemetry.md §4.4): OTLP/JSON, stdlib, no proxy, timestamped at the post. An entry needs "verdict"
   ("pass" or "fail"), "cost_usd" (a number), and "tokens" with "input", "output", "cache_read", and
   "cache_creation" (integers), and a "run" that is its file's name. Only an entry this machine attests is posted;
   the rest wait (PENDING). The history is append-only: a branch that changes or removes an entry fails, and so does
   a malformed entry or a link. A collector that doesn't answer is a WARN.
6. Summary. One line for the merge commit's message, and the merge command, by SHA, with replace objects off.

--host skips the container phase (plan §19: the devcontainer image won't build), and every summary line says
DEGRADED. Lint, tests, the scaffolds, and stage H then run nowhere: never on the host.

--contract-replay FILE is make contract-live's replay (contracts/provider-adapter.md §5.3): the container phase over
`git archive HEAD`, with FILE mounted read-only, running `vitest run test/contract/replay.test.ts` in the gateway
with H4_CONTRACT_RECORDING set and --network none. It passes only when the replay passed tests under the
recording's own name ("recorded live: <adapter>"), so a replay that never read FILE can't pass.

Statuses are make check's (PASS, SKIP, PLANNED, PENDING, FAIL), plus WARN for telemetry that didn't arrive and for
a Claude Code above its floor.
Exit 0 with no FAIL or PENDING; 1 otherwise, or when the export's proof fails; 2 when the gate refuses to start.
"""

